  "reason": "The key surprise in the completed experiments is that RNA-only (config_022, acc=0.5305) outperforms both multimodal configs using scgpt+resnet50 (config_013 acc=0.5121, config_010 acc=0.5251). This suggests the image modality may be adding noise rather than signal. The most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality has any standalone predictive value at all. config_003 (image_only, multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool) is a clean ablation: it uses the same image encoder and aggregation as the multimodal runs but removes the RNA branch entirely. If image-only accuracy is very low, it confirms the image is a noise source and future budget should focus on RNA-only variants (e.g., transformer aggregation, different RNA encoders). If image-only is moderate, the problem lies in fusion, and we should explore alternative fusion/aggregation strategies. This single experiment resolves the dominant uncertainty and directly guides where to allocate the remaining limited budget, making it the highest-information next step."
